Brisbane's student housing market extends well beyond the inner city. The 2032 Olympic infrastructure investment has improved transport and created new housing in suburbs that were previously commuter-only. This guide goes deeper into the affordable outer options.

### South Side Value Zone

**Moorooka & Annerley**: 8 km south of the CBD, on the Beenleigh train line. Multicultural (Moorooka is Brisbane's African quarter), 15 min train to South Bank (QUT/TAFE). Rooms AUD 180–260/week. Excellent cheap eats.

**Salisbury & Coopers Plains**: 12 km south, near Griffith Nathan campus. Older homes on larger blocks, mostly detached houses. 10 min bus to Nathan campus. Rooms AUD 160–240/week. Some of Brisbane's best southern suburb value.

**Mount Gravatt & Upper Mount Gravatt**: Griffith's Mt Gravatt campus and Westfield Garden City. 15–20 min express bus to the CBD. Rooms AUD 180–280/week. Purpose-built student complexes near the campus.

### North Side Value Zone

**Chermside & Aspley**: 12 km north, near the Prince Charles Hospital (medical students). Chermside has Brisbane's largest shopping centre and a new busway station. 20 min express bus to the CBD. Rooms AUD 170–260/week.

**Nundah & Northgate**: 10 km north, on the train line. Nundah Village has a walkable main street with independent cafes. 15 min train to the CBD. Rooms AUD 180–270/week.

### East Side Value Zone

**Cannon Hill & Morningside**: 8 km east, near the Gateway Motorway. 15 min train to the CBD. Rooms AUD 180–260/week.

### Transport & Realistic Commutes

Brisbane's TransLink network (trains, buses, and Brisbane Metro — a new bi-articulated bus system) covers the suburbs well. A student go card reduces fares by 50%. Key commute times:
- Moorooka → South Bank: 15 min train
- Chermside → CBD: 20 min bus (busway — no traffic)
- Mount Gravatt → CBD: 15–20 min express bus

The Brisbane Metro (opening 2025–26) runs 24 hours on weekends — a game-changer for students living in the suburbs.

### FAQ

**Is it worth living that far from campus?** If you save AUD 80–100/week (AUD 4,000–5,000/year) and your commute is 15–20 min by train/busway, yes. Brisbane's busway system means "far" is measured in time, not distance.
**What about flooding?** Check the Brisbane City Council flood maps before renting. The 2022 floods affected many riverside suburbs. Salisbury/Rocklea are flood-prone; Annerley/Moorooka are mostly fine.
**Food scene in the suburbs?** Inala (Vietnamese), Sunnybank (Chinese/Korean/Japanese), and Moorooka (African) have some of Brisbane's best food — and it's cheaper than the inner city.
